    status: "One of the five linked to the incident, whose bodies were never found. No scene shows what became of this child; the model reads the yellow bear as this child's (medium).",
    firstAppearance: "fnaf1", image: "fnaf3-happiest-day.png",
    evidence: ["fnaf1-news-five-children", "fnaf2-give-gifts-give-life", "fnaf3-n5-ghosts-safe-room", "fnaf3-happiest-day", "ffps-lorekeeper-gravestones", "hw2-memory-dolls"],
    theory: "In the seven counts of the dead that the model lists there are four and one more, and in four of the seven the one more is marked by the yellow bear (medium-high for the pattern). In the other three the fifth is there and is not marked as the bear's. Two more scenes show five dead children alike [[fnaf2-save-them]] [[fnaf2-foxy-go-go-go]], and one screen shows four heads and no fifth [[fnaf3-good-ending-heads]]. The model reads the yellow bear, Golden Freddy, as this child's (medium). How and when the child came to it is not shown (low for any mechanism). Whether this child is {{one-you-should-not-have-killed}} of Ultimate Custom Night is argued in ((ucn)), and is not stated as fact anywhere. No name is supplied for this child here. See ((golden)).",
