    theory: "Three readings, and the game settles none. It may be what Pizzeria Simulator's fire left of the salvaged rabbit, since the buried pizzeria is most likely that game's building (low-medium). The model holds that it is not the endoskeleton sealed behind the concrete (medium). The game shows the rabbit itself seizing a machine; that something in the network moves it is low. Who stood the remains in the station is not shown. The jaw is a look and not a finding: nothing shows that any part of it is organic. In a 2024 interview, on record here as a transcript, Scott said that it \"was never supposed to move\" [[scott-2024-interview-burntrap-never-meant-to-move]], and that its name began as a casual planning label [[scott-2024-interview-placeholder-names-canon]]. See ((burntrap)).",
